				<text id="txt1" position="relative" anim="none" margin-bottom="30" margin-top="30"><![CDATA[<div class="row justify-content-center"><div class="col-12 col-md-9 col-lg-7 col-xl-6"><p class="p_result">The answer is heart <em>and</em> bone marrow transplant.</p><p class="text-left p_answer">The world's first successful open-heart procedure was carried out by Dr. F. John Lewis at the University of Minnesota in 1952. Shortly following in 1968, the University successfully completed the world’s first bone marrow transplant, performed by Robert Good, MD. Since then, the University of Minnesota has established itself as a top medical research university, making groundbreaking contributions to the state, the nation, and the world.</p> <p class="text-left p_answer">Home to organizations like the Mayo Clinic, Boston Scientific, Medtronic, and UnitedHealth Group, Minnesota’s medical community is strong and vibrant. Through the <a href="/faculty-research/medical-industry-leadership-institute" target="_blank">Medical Industry Leadership Institute</a> and the <a href="/faculty-research/business-advancement-center-health" target="_blank">Business Advancement Center for Health</a>, the Carlson School plays a big role in preparing the next generation of business leaders to tackle the nation’s biggest health challenges.</p></div></div>]]></text>

